{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:10.1186/1471-2172-9-9 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":6,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"18366814","source":"MED","pmid":"18366814","pmcid":"PMC2275721","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC2275721"]},"doi":"10.1186/1471-2172-9-9","title":"Precision and linearity targets for validation of an IFNgamma ELISPOT, cytokine flow cytometry, and tetramer assay using CMV peptides.","authorString":"Maecker HT, Hassler J, Payne JK, Summers A, Comatas K, Ghanayem M, Morse MA, Clay TM, Lyerly HK, Bhatia S, Ghanekar SA, Maino VC, Delarosa C, Disis ML.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Maecker HT","lastName":"Maecker","firstName":"Holden T","initials":"HT","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"BD Biosciences, San Jose, CA, USA. holden_maecker@sbcglobal.net"}]}},{"fullName":"Hassler J","lastName":"Hassler","firstName":"Jeffrey","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Payne JK","lastName":"Payne","firstName":"Janice K","initials":"JK"},{"fullName":"Summers A","lastName":"Summers","firstName":"Amanda","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Comatas K","lastName":"Comatas","firstName":"Karrie","initials":"K"},{"fullName":"Ghanayem M","lastName":"Ghanayem","firstName":"Manar","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Morse MA","lastName":"Morse","firstName":"Michael A","initials":"MA"},{"fullName":"Clay TM","lastName":"Clay","firstName":"Timothy M","initials":"TM"},{"fullName":"Lyerly HK","lastName":"Lyerly","firstName":"Herbert K","initials":"HK","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0063-4770"}},{"fullName":"Bhatia S","lastName":"Bhatia","firstName":"Sonny","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Ghanekar SA","lastName":"Ghanekar","firstName":"Smita A","initials":"SA"},{"fullName":"Maino VC","lastName":"Maino","firstName":"Vernon C","initials":"VC"},{"fullName":"Delarosa C","lastName":"Delarosa","firstName":"Corazon","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Disis ML","lastName":"Disis","firstName":"Mary L","initials":"ML"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0063-4770"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["protocols"]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"9","journalIssueId":2466099,"dateOfPublication":"2008 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2008,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"BMC Immunol","title":"BMC immunology","essn":"1471-2172","issn":"1471-2172","nlmid":"100966980","isoabbreviation":"BMC Immunol"},"printPublicationDate":"2008-03-01"},"pubYear":"2008","pageInfo":"9","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Single-cell assays of immune function are increasingly used to monitor T cell responses in immunotherapy clinical trials. Standardization and validation of such assays are therefore important to interpretation of the clinical trial data. Here we assess the levels of intra-assay, inter-assay, and inter-operator precision, as well as linearity, of CD8+ T cell IFNgamma-based ELISPOT and cytokine flow cytometry (CFC), as well as tetramer assays.<h4>Results</h4>Precision was measured in cryopreserved PBMC with a low, medium, or high response level to a CMV pp65 peptide or peptide mixture. Intra-assay precision was assessed using 6 replicates per assay; inter-assay precision was assessed by performing 8 assays on different days; and inter-operator precision was assessed using 3 different operators working on the same day. Percent CV values ranged from 4% to 133% depending upon the assay and response level. Linearity was measured by diluting PBMC from a high responder into PBMC from a non-responder, and yielded R2 values from 0.85 to 0.99 depending upon the assay and antigen.<h4>Conclusion</h4>These data provide target values for precision and linearity of single-cell assays for those wishing to validate these assays in their own laboratories. They also allow for comparison of the precision and linearity of ELISPOT, CFC, and tetramer across a range of response levels. There was a trend toward tetramer assays showing the highest precision, followed closely by CFC, and then ELISPOT; while all three assays had similar linearity. These findings are contingent upon the use of optimized protocols for each assay.","affiliation":"BD Biosciences, San Jose, CA, USA. holden_maecker@sbcglobal.net","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NCI NIH HHS","acronym":"CA","grantId":"U54 CA090818","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cytomegalovirus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Peptides","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"AN","qualifierName":"analysis"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Viral Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"AN","qualifierName":"analysis"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Flow Cytometry","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Reproducibility of Results"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Tissue Donors"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Interferon-gamma","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"AN","qualifierName":"analysis"}]}}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Peptides","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Viral Proteins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Interferon-gamma","registryNumber":"82115-62-6"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}